#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# chebyshev_u

#% text
# `chebyshev_u(n, x)` gives the Chebyshev polynomial of the second kind U_n(x).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# At a non-negative integer degree the polynomial is expanded in its argument (evaluated for numbers).

#% item
# At other numeric degrees the hypergeometric representation gives the value; symbolic degrees stay unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
chebyshev_u(3, x)
#% output
#= -4*x + 8*x^3

#% cell
chebyshev_u(3, 0.3)
#% output
#= -0.984

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
chebyshev_u(0.5, 0.3)
#% output
#= 0.9922778767136674

